# TODO

- Nothing in the database forces a visible tree row to have a rank. Every parent is ordered by
  rank alone, so a row revealed or inserted without one sorts by id and refuses drags placed
  relative to it (`stale-anchor`). Only the 0130 migration test and `import-resume.db.test.ts`
  check for it. Enforce it where a new insert path cannot skip it: a CHECK
  `(deleted_at IS NOT NULL OR hidden OR rank IS NOT NULL)` added `NOT VALID` then validated,
  which needs every path that reveals a row (`placeLive`'s land, reveal, restore) to write the
  rank in the same statement that clears `hidden` or `deleted_at`.
